From bcbd121b6510d08ee4579c441abedaeec9cda99c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:40:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a start for another card's monitor asks
 whether to keep it

A monitor of another graphics card, chosen in the settings, is taken by
starting Kodi again (CWinSystemGbm::ChangeScreen()). Kodi's question to keep a
change, with its countdown, could not follow the change across that start: a
display that shows nothing was found out after it, with nothing to undo it.
That is why LibreELEC hides the setting on GBM.

Now the change is noted down before Kodi is started again, where it outlasts
Kodi and a start of the system (the user's data, written whole and synced). If
it cannot be, Kodi is not started for it: the monitor is used from the next
start, as when the user says not now. The start that follows asks "Keep this
monitor?" with a countdown of 15 s. What is not answered yes (no, back, the time
running out, a display that shows nothing, a question that cannot be shown
within 90 s) puts the monitor of before back, and Kodi starts again once more,
on it; that one is asked about too, and where it is not kept either the setting
goes to Default, as at a start where none is named. Two starts at most, then
nothing is left noted down. A question is counted before it is put: a start
that ends while it is open does not keep the monitor (twice at most). Where the
start could not take the monitor chosen (Kodi is on another display), the
setting names the one of before again without a start, and a notification says
so.

Only a change made this way is asked about: what is noted down names the
monitor it chose, and a setting that names another one by the start (changed
by other means: JSON-RPC, guisettings.xml) asks nothing and forgets it. While
the decision gives the setting its value, the window system takes it as it is
(no move, no question). Each step is in the log ("Monitor: ...").

The decisions are in DRMMonitorConfirm.h, with nothing of Kodi in them. Host
test: every step, and 648 runs of every answer at every question with the
monitors taken or not by the start: no loop, two starts at most, the setting
one of the three values, nothing left noted down; 9 mutations caught. The help
of the setting says that the start asks. Texts #39858 to #39861 (Estuary #31729
to #31732) in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx.
